# Gateway config

- Local Phase 1 shape: Docker APISIX on a laptop. Upstream is mock CDP or live Knox from `.env`.
- Prefer `gateway up` / `gateway knox` / `gateway test`. Compose lives in `deploy/docker-compose.yml` with `--project-directory` at the repo root.
- Prefer file-based APISIX config and Compose. Keep Admin API bound to localhost.
- Pin `KNOX_JWKS_URL` host. Allowlist Livy for Spark 3 `GET`/`HEAD` only (`/cdp/livy_for_spark3*`). Allowlist WebHDFS `GET`/`HEAD`/`PUT` (`/cdp/webhdfs*`) for operator staging. Livy writes go through `/mcp/spark`. Do not publish WebHDFS `DELETE`.
- Recreate the `apisix` container when `mock-cdp` is recreated. Stale DNS makes token-state HTTP 404 look like `401 revoked`.
- Put `limit-count` on `/mcp/spark`, `/mcp/hive`, and `/mcp/impala` keyed by Knox `sub` (`knox_user`). Do not burst-cap operator Livy GET or WebHDFS.
- Enable APISIX `key-auth` in `conf/config.yaml` when MCP caller keys are used. Custom `plugins:` lists replace the default set; omitting `key-auth` drops MCP routes.
- Put `key-auth` (`X-Agent-Key`) on `/mcp/spark`, `/mcp/hive`, and `/mcp/impala` when `AGENT_CALLER_KEY` is set. Do not put it on Livy GET or WebHDFS. Hide the caller key from upstreams.
- Publish `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` without JWT. Put `resource_metadata` on knox-jwt `401`. Pin `KNOX_TOKEN_STATE_URL` to `UPSTREAM_HOST`.
- Fail closed: missing/invalid bearer must not reach Knox. Revoked managed tokens (`knox.id`) must not reach Knox when token-state is configured.
- Timeouts should assume long CDP jobs; do not use tiny defaults on probe routes without documenting why.

Do not put tokens, private keys, or real hostnames with credentials in YAML committed to git. Use env substitution from `.env`.
